course: dictionary
lesson: 1788
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and clipper is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. «Barbers use hair clippers for a neat cut.» Hair and cut point to a tool.
explain: «NASA's Europa Clipper launched in 2024 and should reach Jupiter in 2030.» Launched and reach Jupiter are the clues here. They tell you the name is about a spacecraft that travels to a planet, so you do not need the tool meaning.
explain: Check your choice by putting it back into the sentence. If your meaning makes sense every time, you have probably got it right. If it does not, look at the other clues.
fact: A clipper is a tool for cutting hair, nails or hedges, and clippers is the usual plural word.
fact: «Clipper» also means a fast sailing ship from the 1800s, which carried tea and wool across oceans.
fact: A clipper can also mean anything that clips or holds things.
fact: Useful phrases: hair clippers, nail clippers, hedge clippers, clipper ship.
fact: «Sharp clippers are used only with care», so an adult can help you use them safely.
exercise: «Fingernails are cut following their curve, with nail clippers or by an adult.» What are nail clippers used for? | Cleaning shoes | *Cutting fingernails | Carrying water | Painting nails
exercise: «NASA's Europa Clipper launched in 2024 and should reach Jupiter in 2030.» What kind of thing is the Europa Clipper? | A toy car | A fast sailing ship on the sea | A pair of scissors | *A spacecraft sent to Jupiter
exercise: In history lessons, what was a clipper? | A tiny bird | A pair of hair scissors | *A fast sailing ship of the 1800s | A tool for cutting hedges
test: «The barber used hair clippers.» What does clippers mean here? | Tea and wool | Sharp nails | A fast sailing ship | *A tool for cutting hair
test: Clipper ships carried which goods across oceans very fast? | Apples and eggs | Sand and bricks | *Tea and wool | Paper and paint
exam: «Sharp clippers are used only with care.» Why? | They are very heavy | They only work in the sun | They are made of wood | *They can hurt you if handled carelessly
